# Factory

The MaCSad math factory, one program with one role per process. Which role runs
is the first argument:

- `ingest fc <manifest.json> <out>` — the formalization lab's 200 statements;
- `ingest opdp <atlas.json[.gz]> <out> [chunk-mb]` — the OPDP atlas, streamed;
- `verifier judge <statement.lg> <goal> <submission.lg>` — one submission judged;
- `verifier statement <statement.lg> <goal>` — a statement checked well-formed;
- `verifier reference` — the kernel reference checked against the kernel;
- `reference` — the kernel reference, as a model reads it;
- `local <workspace> <problem-id> [attempts]` — the whole loop on one machine:
  prompt, model (replay or OpenRouter), kernel, trail, result;
- `worker` and `coordinator` — the distributed roles, which need the coordinator's
  routes and database first.

Every role prints what it did and exits non-zero when it did not do it.

Import Wire.
Import Shared.
Import Trail.
Import Rank.
Import Submission.
Import Verdict.
Import OpenRouter from "openrouter.lg".
Import Host.
Import Verifier.
Import Replay.
Import Reference.
Import Prompts.
Import IngestFc from "ingest_fc.lg".
Import IngestOpdp from "ingest_opdp.lg".
Import Local.

## Note
How the factory is run.

## To usage () -> Text:
    Return joinLines(["usage: factory <role> …", "  ingest fc <manifest.json> <out-dir>", "  ingest opdp <atlas.json | atlas.json.gz> <out-dir> [chunk-mb]", "  verifier judge <statement.lg> <goal> <submission.lg>", "  verifier statement <statement.lg> <goal>", "  verifier reference", "  reference", "  local <workspace> <problem-id> [attempts]", "  worker | coordinator"]).

## Note
The argument at a position (counting the program's own name as the first), or `""`.

## To argAt (xs: Seq of Text, i: Int) -> Text:
    If i is greater than length of xs:
        Return "".
    Return item i of xs.

## Note
What a role reports: a line for the operator, and whether it did its job.

## An Outcome has:
    a message, which is Text.
    an ok, which is Bool.

## Note
A successful outcome.

## To done (message: Text) -> Outcome:
    Return a new Outcome with message message and ok true.

## Note
A failed outcome.

## To failed (message: Text) -> Outcome:
    Return a new Outcome with message message and ok false.

## Note
The formalization lab's manifest, ingested into `out`.

## To runIngestFc (manifestPath: Text, out: Text) -> Outcome:
    Inspect readText(manifestPath):
        When Err (e):
            Return failed("cannot read the manifest: " + e).
        When Ok (text):
            Inspect ingestManifest(text):
                When Err (e):
                    Return failed(e).
                When Ok (got):
                    Let made be ensureDir(out).
                    Let mutable problemLines be a new Seq of Text.
                    Repeat for p in got's problems:
                        Push toJson_Problem(p) to problemLines.
                    Let mutable nodeLines be a new Seq of Text.
                    Repeat for n in got's nodes:
                        Push toJson_Node(n) to nodeLines.
                    Let w1 be writeAtomically(out + "/problems.jsonl", join(problemLines, "\n") + "\n").
                    Let w2 be writeAtomically(out + "/nodes.jsonl", join(nodeLines, "\n") + "\n").
                    Return done("ingested {length of got's problems} problems and {length of got's nodes} nodes into " + out).
    Return failed("unreachable").

## Note
The OPDP atlas, streamed into `out`, with the time each stage took.

## To runIngestOpdp (atlasPath: Text, out: Text, chunkMb: Int) -> Outcome:
    Let t0 be clockMs().
    Inspect prepareAtlas(atlasPath, out + "/work", chunkMb):
        When Err (e):
            Return failed(e).
        When Ok (chunks):
            Let t1 be clockMs().
            Inspect ingestAtlasChunks(chunks, out, "UnsolvedMath"):
                When Err (e):
                    Return failed(e).
                When Ok (s):
                    Let t2 be clockMs().
                    Let mutable line be "cohort {s's cohort}: declared {s's declared}, scanned {s's scanned}, written {s's written}, refused {s's refused}; {s's chunks} chunks, {s's bytes} bytes; prepare {t1 - t0} ms, scan {s's scanMs} ms, project {s's projectMs} ms, write {s's writeMs} ms, total {t2 - t0} ms".
                    If s's firstRefusal is not equal to "":
                        Set line to line + "; first refusal: " + s's firstRefusal.
                    If s's declared is at least 0 and s's declared is not equal to s's scanned:
                        Return failed(line + "; the atlas declares a different number of records than it holds").
                    Return done(line).
    Return failed("unreachable").

## Note
One submission file judged against one statement file.

## To runJudge (statementPath: Text, goal: Text, submissionPath: Text) -> Outcome:
    Inspect readText(statementPath):
        When Err (e):
            Return failed("cannot read the statement: " + e).
        When Ok (statement):
            Inspect readText(submissionPath):
                When Err (e):
                    Return failed("cannot read the submission: " + e).
                When Ok (submission):
                    Let v be judgeSubmission(defaultToolchain(), statement, goal, submission).
                    Let line be toJson_Verdict(v).
                    If v's kind is equal to "verified":
                        Return done(line).
                    Return failed(line).
    Return failed("unreachable").

## Note
One statement file checked well-formed.

## To runStatementCheck (statementPath: Text, goal: Text) -> Outcome:
    Inspect readText(statementPath):
        When Err (e):
            Return failed("cannot read the statement: " + e).
        When Ok (statement):
            Let v be judgeStatement(defaultToolchain(), statement, goal).
            If v's kind is equal to "verified":
                Return done(toJson_Verdict(v)).
            Return failed(toJson_Verdict(v)).
    Return failed("unreachable").

## Note
The kernel reference checked against the kernel.

## To runReferenceCheck () -> Outcome:
    Let problems be referenceProblems(defaultToolchain()).
    If length of problems is equal to 0:
        Return done("every one of the {length of allExamples()} reference examples is what the kernel says it is, and every promised prelude name is bound").
    Return failed(join(problems, "\n")).

## Note
The role the arguments name, run.

## To dispatch (xs: Seq of Text) -> Outcome:
    Let role be argAt(xs, 2).
    Let sub be argAt(xs, 3).
    If role is equal to "ingest" and sub is equal to "fc" and length of xs is at least 5:
        Return runIngestFc(argAt(xs, 4), argAt(xs, 5)).
    If role is equal to "ingest" and sub is equal to "opdp" and length of xs is at least 5:
        Let mutable chunkMb be 32.
        If length of xs is at least 6:
            Set chunkMb to parseInt(argAt(xs, 6)).
        Return runIngestOpdp(argAt(xs, 4), argAt(xs, 5), chunkMb).
    If role is equal to "verifier" and sub is equal to "judge" and length of xs is at least 6:
        Return runJudge(argAt(xs, 4), argAt(xs, 5), argAt(xs, 6)).
    If role is equal to "verifier" and sub is equal to "statement" and length of xs is at least 5:
        Return runStatementCheck(argAt(xs, 4), argAt(xs, 5)).
    If role is equal to "verifier" and sub is equal to "reference":
        Return runReferenceCheck().
    If role is equal to "reference":
        Return done(kernelReference()).
    If role is equal to "local" and length of xs is at least 4:
        Let mutable attempts be 1.
        If length of xs is at least 5:
            Set attempts to parseInt(argAt(xs, 5)).
        Return runLocal(argAt(xs, 3), argAt(xs, 4), attempts).
    If role is equal to "worker" or role is equal to "coordinator":
        Return failed("the {role} role needs the coordinator's routes and database, which are not built yet; use `local`.\n" + usage()).
    Return failed(usage()).

## Main

Let outcome be dispatch(programArgs()).
Show outcome's message.
If outcome's ok is equal to false:
    Fail with "the role did not complete".

## Test: no arguments print the usage and fail

Let o be dispatch(["factory"]).
Expect that o's ok is equal to false.
Expect that o's message is equal to usage().

## Test: the distributed roles say what they need

Let o be dispatch(["factory", "worker"]).
Expect that o's ok is equal to false.
Expect that o's message contains "the worker role needs the coordinator's routes and database".

## Test: the reference role prints the reference

Let o be dispatch(["factory", "reference"]).
Expect that o's ok is equal to true.
Expect that o's message is equal to kernelReference().

## Test: ingest fc reads a manifest from the sealed filesystem and writes the graph

Let w be writeText("manifest.json", sampleManifest()).
Let o be dispatch(["factory", "ingest", "fc", "manifest.json", "out"]).
Expect that o's ok is equal to true.
Expect that o's message is equal to "ingested 2 problems and 5 nodes into out".
Inspect readText("out/problems.jsonl"):
    When Ok (t):
        Expect that length of lines(trimEnd(t)) is equal to 2.
    When Err (e):
        Expect that e is equal to "readable".

## Test: an argument past the end is empty

Expect that argAt(["a"], 2) is equal to "".
Expect that argAt(["a", "b"], 2) is equal to "b".
